docs/history/v1/traceability/ieee1722_1-2021.md:290:| CMD-15 | 7.4.40 | GET_AVB_INFO (gPTP GM, propagation delay, domain, flags, MSRP mappings) | processor getter plus the root Milan-info face | ✅ IMPLEMENTED at `0x0055`. The response serves the root's grandmaster identity, effective propagation delay, domain and asCapable plus the processor's SR class-A priority/VLAN mapping and AVTP-down flag. One root snapshot comparator observes the same values served on a later solicited read and drives the Table 5.22 notification. Processor `pp_top` and root `[NOTIFY]` wire tests grade the success body and change/content parity. | 7.4.40 is the one-shot network-health view BENCH reads; stale GM here contradicts ADP (ADP-9). |
docs/history/v1/traceability/ieee1722_1-2021.md:291:| CMD-15a | 7.4.40.2 | **A non-success GET_AVB_INFO response keeps the 20-byte minimum payload** (type+index+gm_id+propagation_delay+domain+flags+msrp_mappings_count), count = 0. Equality with the SUCCESS size is NOT the rule here — the mapping list is variable-length. **L4** — oracle: la_avdecc `AecpAemGetAvbInfoResponsePayloadMinSize` = 20 (clause-tagged) and the reference device, MEASURED answering its error with cdl 32 exactly | processor getter | 🟡 **FUNCTION IMPLEMENTED; NON-SUCCESS SIZE RULE UNPROVEN.** `pp_top` grades the byte-exact variable-length success body and the expected statuses for missing, unsupported, and truncated requests, but the present checks do not independently assert the 20-byte minimum body and `cdl` 32 on each non-success path. Do not promote this row without that wire-length assertion. | 7.4.40.2: same drop-on-short-response class as CMD-7b, on the command Hive reads for network health. |
docs/history/v1/traceability/milan-v12.md:225:| M-AECP-10 | 5.4.5.2 (Table 5.22) | Unsolicited notifications for every listed state change, plus command-specific success notifications | `KL_aecp_notify` (registry, scheduler, per-descriptor counter limiter), the microprograms' `NOTIFY_ENQ`, and the root's answer-matched counter, GET_AVB_INFO and GET_AS_PATH comparators in `milan_datapath` | ✅ IMPLEMENTED at 0x0055 (issue #69). Successful state-changing commands push to every registered controller except the requester; no-op SETs are silent. GET_AVB_INFO snapshot-compares the GM identity, effective propagation delay, domain and asCapable while the processor observes its remaining served fields. GET_AS_PATH compares exactly `(count ? GM : 0, count, active tails)`. Product fabric mode preserves the donor's standards-defined no-TLV count zero: fabric 0 <-> 1 changes the served empty/`[GM]` sequence, while GM A->B with both counts zero is AS_PATH-silent but still drives GET_AVB_INFO and `GPTP_GM_CHANGED`. Only option-off retains #227's raw count-0/1 GM-only alias; every owner aliases to empty while GM=0. The first-count gather snapshots conditional GM/count/tails, so a response is wholly old or wholly new. Evidence: `protocol-processor/tb/aecp_notify` and `protocol-processor/tb/pp_top`; fabric `tb/verilator/milan_dp/sim_gptp.cpp` grades no-TLV response geometry, generation/push polarity, absent GM switching, explicit `[GM]`, and an in-flight withdrawal; the option-off `[NOTIFY]` leg grades its alias, atomic publication and deterministic interleave. Domain-only changes reach GET_AVB_INFO, never AS_PATH or `GPTP_GM_CHANGED`. | The declared CRF Stream Input serves no counters and therefore has no counter push (audit B4). |
